    "topic_geometry_measure_intro": "For learners and makers who need area, length, slope, volume, or unit conversion without opening CAD. Use these when the geometry is simple and you can name the inputs (sides, radius, rise/run, from-unit/to-unit).",
    "topic_geometry_measure_choose_title": "Picking a geometry or unit tool",
    "topic_geometry_measure_choose_body": "If you have a named shape, open triangle, circle, volume, or Pythagorean helpers. For grades and ramps, use slope or gradient. For screens and crops, use aspect ratio. For “how many cm in…”, use the unit converter. Room-material takeoffs (paint/tile/concrete) live primarily under home-diy even when area math overlaps.",
