    "topic_time_calendar_desc": "Age, date difference, time-zone conversion, and Unix timestamps for planning and engineering—clear on leap years, offsets, and UTC versus local time.",
    "topic_time_calendar_blurb": "Dates, age, time zones, and Unix time for everyone from trip planners to engineers debugging timestamps.",
    "topic_time_calendar_intro": "For anyone answering “how old,” “how many days between,” “what time is it there,” or “what UTC instant is this epoch.” Engineers get first-class Unix and zone helpers; consumers get age and span math without spreadsheet gymnastics.",
    "topic_time_calendar_choose_title": "Which time tool fits?",
    "topic_time_calendar_choose_body": "Use age for birthday-based spans, date difference for booking or project length, timezone converter for meetings across regions, and Unix timestamp when APIs or logs speak epoch seconds/millis. Say whether you mean calendar days or exact 24-hour durations when contracts care.",
    "topic_time_calendar_limits_title": "Boundaries",
    "topic_time_calendar_limits_body": "Civil time is messy: DST transitions, canceled leap seconds in some APIs, and historical calendar reforms can surprise you. Legal deadlines may use business-day calendars these tools do not encode. Always confirm the zone ID (not only a city nickname) for critical meetings.",
    "topic_time_calendar_faq_q1": "Why does age differ by a day near birthdays?",
